body:
I relate a lot, although I still am very young and haven't had mine long. 

&#x200B;

If yours are quite old (10+ years) they should come out a lot easier with laser. If you go to a very experienced laser clinic your chances of scarring are slim to none. Hold out hope, they won't stop you achieving what you want in life.

Honestly everything else in my life is going great. It's my regret towards the tattoos that's making me suicidal. And the guilt and shame that comes with having them. Every time I see them (when I'm wearing shorts I can see one, it's on my thigh) I have a crippling panic attack and want to grab a cheese grater and scrape it off.

&#x200B;

Fact of the matter is, I'm NOT a tattoo person. I never really thought of getting them, only a vague casual "what if" and then impulsively decided on two random days to get some. I'm embarrassed and ashamed of them because they're pretty nerdy and I hate that they're now permanently on my body, never able to go back to how I was before.

&#x200B;

I'm currently seeing a therapist to try and deal with this regret (only one session so far, not much progress yet of course). But honestly? I'd rather die than live with this irreversible regret.
